# Human-Readable Skill Name

State the outcome this skill should produce and the intent boundary it must preserve. Assume Codex already knows general software-engineering practices; include only guidance that changes decisions or prevents realistic failures.

## Workflow

- Establish scope, evidence, constraints, and the observable completion condition.
- Use the narrowest reliable tools and preserve repository-specific instructions.
- Separate verified facts, inferences, and unresolved user decisions.
- Make external or destructive changes only when the request authorizes them.
- Verify the result in proportion to risk and report unavailable checks honestly.

## Output

Define the decision, artifact, or evidence the skill must return. Add modes, references, scripts, or examples only when they materially improve repeated use.
